  "title": "1898 novel 'Futility' eerily mirrors Titanic disaster",
  "description": "In 1898 Morgan Robertson wrote a novella about the ocean liner Titan that sank after hitting an iceberg. Fourteen years later the real RMS Titanic suffered the same fate, sparking rumors of prophecy. This short explains how the novel’s details matched reality and why the similarities are rooted in maritime knowledge, not clairvoyance.\n\nExplore the uncanny parallels and the lasting myth behind Futility.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"The Wreck of the Titan: Or, Futility\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Titan:_Or,_Futility), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.",
